                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0fb077a3-89e9-32c3-b723-37643ae4e8d2",
                        "entry_id": "e3063f00-de48-3c8f-ba65-a8784424f53c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ancient Roman praenomen."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e02937b-5259-475d-9343-451a1285af82",
                                "sense_id": "0fb077a3-89e9-32c3-b723-37643ae4e8d2",
                                "text": "The two Plinys, Lucan, (though again under the disadvantage of verse) Petronius Arbiter, and Quintilian, but above all, the Senecas, (for a Spanish cross appears to improve the quality of the rhetorician) have left a body of rhetorical composition such as no modern nation has rivalled."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af23c420-09cf-411c-9034-bde848e08a3d",
                                "sense_id": "0fb077a3-89e9-32c3-b723-37643ae4e8d2",
                                "text": "Of Q. Curtius, the Demosthenes (both), Eutropius, Horace (first with a date), Homer, Justin, Livy, the two Plinies, Quintilian, Martial, Tacitus, and Virgil, the first editions; but my friend must not be allowed to have a succession of nights of undisturbed repose till he possesses the first Horace, and the first Roman edition of Virgil."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d72e325e-c613-394f-8b0d-41913caad900",
                        "entry_id": "e3063f00-de48-3c8f-ba65-a8784424f53c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pliny the Elder, Gaius Plinius Secundus (23–79 AD): an ancient Roman nobleman, scientist and historian, author of Naturalis Historia, \\\"Pliny's Natural History\\\"."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ee03a47-6de8-44df-8468-bb170851ad58",
                                "sense_id": "d72e325e-c613-394f-8b0d-41913caad900",
                                "text": "I will leave off all my childish fooleries and diversions, and set about studying with such a rage, that when you come back next year, you may find the tongue I have now in my mouth more forky than that of some serpents mentioned by Pliny the naturalist."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c6101579-d2eb-3442-8cc8-f37f0f74fd2b",
                        "entry_id": "e3063f00-de48-3c8f-ba65-a8784424f53c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pliny the Younger, Gaius Plinius Caecilius Secundus (63–circa 113): an ancient Roman statesman, orator, and writer, a great-nephew of Pliny the Elder."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
